        // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        [("extraversion_low", "melatonin")] = "MT1/MT2 receptor hypersensitivity in suprachiasmatic nucleus drives early evening withdrawal and powerful circadian pull toward solitary retreat. Pineal NAT-HIOMT pathway activates biological shutdown of external engagement — quiet dark rooms and solo evening rituals as non-negotiable restorative process. Light-dark cycle entrainment strongly favors hermit-mode recharge over late-night socializing.",
        [("extraversion_low", "gaba")] = "GABA-A ionotropic fast inhibition through PV+ interneuron networks actively suppresses social approach circuits in nucleus accumbens. Tonic GABAergic inhibition in amygdala dampens all social reward signaling — behavioral inhibition system dominates over approach motivation. Benzodiazepine-site sensitivity creates natural sedative calm that makes solitary stillness deeply satisfying.",
        [("extraversion_low", "acetylcholine")] = "Muscarinic M1 receptor activation in dorsolateral PFC sustains deep solitary concentration — nucleus basalis cholinergic projections allocate full attentional bandwidth to internal processing, books, and focused thought. Social conversation depletes cholinergic signal-to-noise ratio needed for rich inner life. Parasympathetic vagal tone supports quiet contemplative states over social arousal.",
        [("extraversion_low", "dynorphin")] = "KOR Gi-coupled aversive signaling on VTA dopamine terminals generates powerful social fatigue after group exposure. Prodynorphin expression in NAc drives opponent-process withdrawal from social reward — the neurochemical mechanism of needing to be alone after parties. Kappa-opioid receptor activation creates dysphoria specifically tied to social overstimulation, redirecting all motivation toward solitary recovery.",
        [("extraversion_low", "progesterone")] = "Allopregnanolone positive allosteric modulation at GABA-A receptors creates sedating neurosteroid calm aligned with low-stimulation sanctuary preference. Evening progesterone rise potentiates inhibitory tone that makes quiet rooms and solo activities feel deeply restorative. Social noise experienced as metabolically costly intrusion on peaceful default mode processing.",
        [("extraversion_low", "cortisol")] = "GR low-affinity receptor activation in amygdala during social evaluation creates HPA axis stress cascade — cortisol-ACTH feedback loop treats group exposure and scrutiny as genuine physiological stressor. CRH-cortisol mobilization drives withdrawal toward safe solitary environments where allostatic load can recover.",
        [("extraversion_low", "substance_p")] = "NK1 receptor overactivation in amygdala amplifies aversive emotional pain from social scrutiny and forced group engagement. Substance P release during unwanted social interaction creates visceral discomfort — the neurochemical cost of being trapped in crowds. Social evaluation sensitivity as tachykinin-mediated distress signal.",
        [("extraversion_low", "crh")] = "CRHR1 activation in bed nucleus of stria terminalis generates anticipatory anxiety specifically about social performance demands. CRH hypersecretion from paraventricular nucleus drives avoidance of gatherings and preference for solitary planning — social situations activate the same stress master switch as threat detection.",
        [("extraversion_low", "prolactin")] = "Tuberoinfundibular prolactin release produces rapid social satiation after minimal exposure. Dopamine-prolactin balance shifted so that brief connection satisfies all affiliative need — content to withdraw and recharge alone once small social dose is met. Extended group interaction triggers prolactin-mediated motivational suppression.",

